 ## Overview
-VF-Ray-GPU is a GPGPU implementation of the VF-Ray algorithm designed for memory-efficient ray casting on unstructured tetrahedral volumes [S1]. It solves the problem of rendering large datasets on GPUs with limited memory by avoiding explicit adjacency structures (like `Use_set`) and pre-computed normals, instead computing face parameters and volume integrals on-the-fly [S1]. It sets itself apart from its parent, Visible Faces Driven Ray Casting, by fully parallelizing the visibility determination, projection, and ray traversal across CUDA kernels, utilizing a hash-based local memory buffer for traversal state to minimize global memory bandwidth [S1].
+VF-Ray-GPU is a GPGPU implementation of the VF-Ray algorithm designed for memory-efficient ray casting on unstructured tetrahedral volumes [S1]. It solves the problem of rendering large datasets on GPUs with limited memory by avoiding explicit adjacency structures (like `Use_set`) and pre-computed normals, instead computing face parameters and volume integrals on-the-fly [S1]. It sets itself apart from its parent, Visible Faces Driven Ray Casting, by fully parallelizing the visibility determination, projection, and ray traversal across three CUDA kernels, utilizing a hash-based local memory buffer for traversal state to minimize global memory bandwidth [S1].
 
